WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:07.299 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  sterling is composed of ninety two point  five percent silver and 7.5 percent  alloy the alloy is usually copper or  copper combined with other metals this  manufacturer pours the standard ratio of  alloy and pure silver into a stainless  steel mold the silver rapidly cools and  hardens into a flat bar workers send the  bar between two rollers which apply over  3,300 pounds of pressure workers feed  the bar through the press repeatedly  each time turning the wheel to narrow  the gap between the rollers to  progressively thin out the silver bar  rolling the silver bar makes it riddle  so they reheat it to restore its  flexibility and malleability the bar now  goes through another rolling press  reducing the thickness even more  [Music]  in doing so it lengthens the silver bar  dramatically from 10 inches to 4 yards  the strip now passes through a series of  forming rollers which progressively  curls the edges up and inward until the  strut becomes a hollow tube then the  Machine solder the edges sealing the  tube the tube is still too thick for  making earrings and rings so it goes to  another thinning operation this machine  grabs one end of the tube and pulls it  through a series of circular dies which  have progressively narrower diameters  once the tube is the required diameter a  winding machine curves it to make hoop  earrings an artisan steadies a piece of  curved tube and locking tweezers he  sutter's on an earring hook then a latch  into which the hook snaps some pieces of  jewelry incorporate cubic zirconia  stones in this design a computer has  already cut to pattern pieces out of an  ultra-thin silver sheet and rounded the  sheets into half spheres the artisan  solder is the two halves together  encasing the cubic zirconia stones  inside the rest of the earring  components are made from silver tubing  and silver wire here an artisan is  making a pendant he locks cubic zirconia  stones in between the front and back  frame pieces then he positions the  center piece within the frame soldering  it in four spots he satyrs a ring to the  top of the pendant and the loop for the  chain called the bail next a rotating  barrel of abrasive powder rounds the  edges and smooth rough spots a buffing  with a cloth wheel then polishes the  silver to a mirror finish the same  computerized laser machine that cut the  sphere earrings can also act an  elaborate design on the surface of the  piece it can reproduce virtually any  image that can be created with software  the laser draws by pulverizing a micro  layer of silver as the laser works a  built-in suction device vacuums the  silver powder away besides adding  strength and durability the alloy makes  sterling silver shinier the copper in  particular has anti corrosive properties  which resists tarnishing

